From a824211da17fb5ac810fecdf30ef8c262e6061f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:23:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Port RC-Cockpit's pilot-head gaze servo (piloten.cpp) to
 RP2350 hardware_pwm

Single-servo adaptation of the two-servo Arduino original, matching the
Core2350B's one pilot-head servo. Keeps the same random-timing/easing
gaze FSM and roll-dependent look-into-the-turn bias; only the output
stage changed from the Arduino Servo library to raw hardware_pwm,
replicating its default 0-180 degree -> 544-2400us pulse mapping so
the physical motion matches the original build.

Wired into cockpit_task: pilotenBegin() once at startup, pilotenSetRoll()
+ three pilotenUpdate() calls per frame (before rendering and after each
panel push), adapted from the original's five-calls-across-four-panels
pattern to this board's two panels.
---
